""",
        "en" to """
See where you stopped|When you look at unfinished work, it is easy to see only what is missing. Yet what you learned along the way is still yours. Today is not about settling a debt; it is about understanding where you are.|If you like, write two lines: “I got this far…” and “I stopped here…” No explanation or apology is required.
Find your own reason|You do not have to want everything you once wanted. Sometimes beginning again means putting down someone else’s expectations. Notice which real need this goal meets in your life now.|Finish “I want to return to this because…” If the answer is only to please someone, consider making the goal smaller or letting it go.
Lower the threshold|If starting feels enormous, you may be carrying the whole task to the doorway. Opening the file, putting on your shoes or writing the first question is part of starting too. Small does not mean worthless; it means reachable.|Choose a beginning you can do in two minutes. Do only that; continuing today is optional.
Prepare one place|Willpower does not have to tackle every obstacle alone. Finding what you need, clearing a little space or leaving tomorrow’s first step in sight can make returning easier.|Remove one obstacle: prepare the file, put the book on the table or get your materials out. Preparation may be enough today.
Make room for a missed day|A day that did not go as planned does not invalidate the whole attempt. Doubling the work you missed can make returning harder. You can start somewhere that fits today without settling yesterday’s score.|Choose the next suitable moment and repeat only your small beginning. Do not add a debt to make up for.
Notice a small piece of evidence|Progress does not always look like finished work. Asking for help sooner, removing an unnecessary step or understanding where you struggle also leaves you with useful knowledge. Look at your process as well as your result.|Write one concrete difference from this week: what did you do, learn or make easier? Describe it without comparing yourself to anyone.
